        <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8 leading-tight">AI Customer Support Agent Cost in Australia: What to Expect in 2026</h1>
        <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none font-sans text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          
          <p>AI customer support agents — chatbots trained on your specific business knowledge that can answer customer questions, handle bookings, and escalate complex issues to a human — are one of the fastest-growing AI investments for Australian businesses in 2026. The question we get asked most often is: what does it actually cost?</p>
          <p>The honest answer is that it varies significantly depending on the complexity of your support requirements, the volume of interactions, and whether you're using an off-the-shelf platform or a custom-built solution. This guide breaks it down.</p>
          <h2>Off-the-Shelf AI Support Platforms ($200–$2,000/month)</h2>
          <p>Platforms like Intercom, Zendesk AI, Freshdesk, and Tidio offer AI-powered chat agents that you can configure without writing code. You connect them to your website, upload your knowledge base (FAQs, product documentation, policies), and the AI handles common questions. These platforms typically cost $200–$2,000/month depending on the number of seats, conversation volume, and AI features included.</p>
          <p>The limitation is that these platforms are generic. They're designed for the average support use case, which means they work well for straightforward enquiries but struggle with industry-specific terminology, complex multi-step processes, or integration with your specific software stack (e.g., pulling a customer's job status from ServiceM8 or their order history from a custom ERP).</p>
          <h2>Custom AI Support Agents ($12,000–$40,000 build fee)</h2>
          <p>A custom AI support agent is trained specifically on your business — your products, your policies, your terminology, your customer base. It integrates with your existing systems so it can look up real data (not just static FAQs), and it's designed around your specific support workflows. Custom agents typically cost $12,000–$40,000 to build, with ongoing hosting costs of $300–$1,000/month.</p>
          <p>At PresciaIQ, our AI customer support agents are built on a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) architecture, which means the AI retrieves relevant information from your knowledge base in real time rather than relying on a static training dataset. This keeps the agent accurate as your business evolves without requiring expensive retraining.</p>
          <h2>The ROI Calculation</h2>
          <p>A well-built AI support agent typically handles 50–70% of inbound support enquiries without human intervention. For a business receiving 200 support contacts per week at an average handling time of 8 minutes and a fully-loaded staff cost of $35/hour, that's roughly $37,000 per year in support costs. An agent that handles 60% of those contacts saves $22,000/year — paying back a $15,000 build fee in under 9 months.</p>
          <p>The other ROI driver is availability. An AI agent handles enquiries at 2am on a Sunday with the same quality as 9am on a Monday. For businesses where after-hours enquiries are common — trades, hospitality, e-commerce — the conversion value of capturing those leads is often larger than the cost savings.</p>
          <p>To get a specific ROI estimate for your business, <a href="/start" class="text-primary hover:underline">book a free scoping call</a>.</p>
        
